 R←Test_Misc_010(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;res
⍝ Runs <U.RunProcess> against a process whose output ends in CRLF. The split tested for
⍝ `⎕UCS 10 13` - that is LF,CR - while CRLF is 13,10, so plain CRLF output was split on LF alone
⍝ and every line kept a trailing CR. Output containing a blank line matched and was split into
⍝ garbage. An empty result also has to honour the documented "vector of lines".
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed
 :If 'Win'≢A.GetOperatingSystem ⍬
     R←T._WindowsOnly ⋄ →0
 :EndIf

 res←G.U.RunProcess'cmd.exe' '/c echo Hello'
 →T.PassesIf 1=≢res.StdOut
 →T.PassesIf'Hello'≡∊res.StdOut                 ⍝ No carriage return left over

 res←G.U.RunProcess'cmd.exe' '/c echo a&echo.&echo b'
 →T.PassesIf 3=≢res.StdOut                      ⍝ The blank line in the middle survives as a line
 →T.PassesIf(,'a')≡,⊃res.StdOut
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢2⊃res.StdOut                   ⍝ The blank line is a line of its own
 →T.PassesIf(,'b')≡,⊃⌽res.StdOut

 res←G.U.RunProcess'cmd.exe' '/c rem'
 →T.PassesIf(0⍴⊂'')≡res.StdOut                  ⍝ Still a vector of lines, not a simple ''

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
